## `@mezzanine-ui/react@1.9.0`

> The `Calendar` footer shortcut can now be relabelled, and it no longer lets users pick a disabled period ([#521](https://github.com/Mezzanine-UI/mezzanine/issues/521)).

---

### 🚀 Improvements

- **`Calendar`** — New `calendarFooterControlProps` prop customises the footer shortcut (`Today`, `This month`, …), alongside the other `calendar*Props` bundles. The label was previously a fixed English string. `children` takes a string for every mode, or a per-mode map that overrides the listed modes and keeps the default label for the rest. `CalendarFooterControl` also gains a `disabled` prop, and `CalendarFooterControlProps` is now exported.

  Pickers reach it through `calendarProps`. Prefer a map there, because the footer follows the panel the user drills down to:

  ```tsx
  // Define it outside the render so the object stays stable.
  const calendarProps = {
    calendarFooterControlProps: {
      children: { day: '今天', month: '本月', year: '今年' },
    },
  };

  <DatePicker calendarProps={calendarProps} onChange={setDate} value={date} />;
  ```

### 🐛 Bug Fixes

- **`Calendar`** — The footer shortcut is now disabled when the current period is disabled. It used to ignore the `is*Disabled` predicates, so it could pick a date the board showed as disabled. The check combines the predicates the same way the cells of each mode do *(via `core@1.3.0`)*.

---

**Compatibility**: requires `react` ≥ 19, `react-dom` ≥ 19, `@mezzanine-ui/core` ≥ 1.3.0, `@mezzanine-ui/system` ≥ 1.0.2, `@mezzanine-ui/icons` ≥ 1.0.2

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Mezzanine-UI/mezzanine/compare/@mezzanine-ui/react@1.8.1...@mezzanine-ui/react@1.9.0
